/**
 * Slide 1 of the driver carousel: one job, one route.
 *
 * NOT A FIGMA EXPORT. The Figma frame for this slide was an abstract diagram — two numbered dots
 * joined by a dashed line. This replaces it with the scene the slide is actually about: a truck
 * takes one green route past three farms, picks up at each, and drops the lot at the wholesaler.
 * A driver deciding whether this work is worth owning a vehicle for is being shown the day, not a
 * diagram of it.
 *
 * In its own module because it is 53 KB of path data — an order of magnitude more than the other
 * two slides put together, and `illustrations.tsx` stops being readable with it inline.
 *
 * TWO THINGS WERE CHANGED FROM THE SOURCE SVG, both because react-native-svg is not a browser:
 * `<title>` / `<desc>` and the ARIA attributes were dropped (it renders neither, and warns on
 * elements it does not know), and the `font-family` on the four labels was pointed at
 * `NotoSans_700Bold` — the face `lib/i18n/fonts.ts` actually loads, where `Inter` would have
 * silently fallen back. Everything else, including the `<pattern>` plaid on the third farmer's
 * shirt, is the file as delivered.
 *
 * KNOWN GAP: "Pickup 1 / 2 / 3" and "DROP!" are drawn into the artwork in English, so they do
 * not translate — every other string on this screen does (LP-91). Fixing it properly means
 * lifting the four labels out as React Native <Text> positioned over the scene, which is how the
 * slide this replaced handled its numbered badges. Worth doing before the Sinhala and Tamil copy
 * is reviewed.
 */

